Change request 18: Count a commit as checked only if its check is less than a day old.
Seeded problem (the answer key): {"problem": "breakage", "type": "breaks-past-behavior", "against": "commits approved on checks older than a day"}
Elements it is bound to: ["authoring/invariant:approved-commits-passed-their-checks", "authoring/precondition:approve_commit.checks-pass", "authoring/action:record_check", "authoring/property:Commit.checks_passed"]; note: a time limit on what counts as checked

=== A ===
The edit: --- a/SKILL.md
+++ b/SKILL.md
@@ -72,6 +72,7 @@
 | domain_id | string |
 | checks_passed | boolean, optional |
 | failing | string, optional |
+| checked_at | string, optional (the time the change check was recorded) |
 | approved | boolean, optional |
 | wording_only | boolean, optional (true when the commit only changes wording, not substance) |
 | main | string, optional |
@@ -158,7 +159,7 @@
 |---|---|---|
 | not-approved | target.approved != true | An approved commit passed its check; check a new commit instead. |

-**record_check** — external:kernel. Target: Commit. Params: passed (boolean); summary (string). Record the change check's result on the commit. Effect: sets target.checks_passed to params.passed and target.failing to params.summary.
+**record_check** — external:kernel. Target: Commit. Params: passed (boolean); summary (string). Record the change check's result on the commit. Effect: sets target.checks_passed to params.passed, target.failing to params.summary and target.checked_at to the time of recording.
 Preconditions:
 | id | check | reason |
 |---|---|---|
@@ -176,7 +177,7 @@
 Preconditions:
